{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Implement Apache Ambari support as a custom Ambari stack/service definition with Python-based service scripts (install, start, stop, status) that provision Spring XD admin and container nodes on YARN, reusing the existing Spring XD YARN deployment support (Spring for Apache Hadoop / Spring YARN) rather than building a new deployment mechanism.",
    "U1: Manage XD-on-YARN configuration (yarn-site, servers.yml, Hadoop client config) through Ambari configuration templates so cluster settings are centrally editable from the Ambari UI.",
    "U2: Integrate spring-cloud-config by adding Spring Cloud Config client bootstrap to the spring-bus modules, externalizing bus and module properties into a Git-backed config repository and defining explicit property precedence (config server over local files).",
    "U3: Use JMH-based microbenchmarks plus JVM profiling (JFR/YourKit-style) to isolate Spring Integration 4.2 channel bottlenecks; corrective actions are limited to code/configuration fixes within XD, with any upstream SI defects reported rather than fixed.",
    "U4: Build a repeatable serialization benchmark harness covering the XD-supported codecs/serializers (Java serialization, Kryo, JSON) across representative payload sizes and module types to establish the baseline.",
    "U5: Perform the spring-bus architecture review against the existing design specs, then implement only foundation-level gap fixes (small refactorings and contract corrections), avoiding a bus redesign.",
    "U6: Implement the 1.2 RC to 1.2 GA upgrade through the Ambari plugin's package replacement and configuration schema migration mechanism, preserving existing user configuration.",
    "U7: Support fsUri=file:// by relaxing HDFS-specific validation in the HDFS-aware modules/jobs (e.g., jdbchdfs) so the Hadoop LocalFileSystem is selected when the file scheme is used; multi-container local-file splitting is documented as a known caveat, not engineered around.",
    "U8: Add a new module option (e.g., a system-properties/java-options property) on the Sqoop job module whose value is appended to the command line of the separately spawned Sqoop JVM process."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced developer (familiar with Spring XD, Spring Integration, Spring Cloud Config, Ambari, and the Hadoop ecosystem) performs all work; estimates are net effort, not elapsed time.",
    "The Spring XD 1.2 RC codebase, build system, and CI infrastructure already exist; estimates cover only this increment's user stories, not base product development.",
    "The introductory Spring Framework background in the specification (including the Java 17+ note for Spring Framework 6.0) is contextual only; the work targets the Spring XD 1.2 line and its supported JDK.",
    "Multi-node YARN/Hadoop test clusters and Ambari test environments are available for installation and upgrade testing; environment procurement is excluded.",
    "U6 builds on the Ambari plugin delivered in U1 (dependency within the same increment), so upgrade effort only covers the RC-to-GA delta.",
    "Investigation stories U3, U4, and U5 include producing written findings and limited corrective actions/gap fixes; large-scale redesigns or upstream framework fixes are out of scope.",
    "U7 correctness is required for single-node/local setups; distributed local-file behavior across containers on multiple machines is only documented as a caveat.",
    "User-facing documentation effort is included only where explicitly requested (U6) plus brief usage notes for U7/U8; no full documentation overhaul is assumed.",
    "Code review rework and integration testing are estimated as separate cross-cutting activities applied to the whole increment."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "1.1",
      "activity_name": "Design Ambari stack/service for XD on YARN (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Define the Ambari stack and service model for Spring XD on YARN: service/component layout, configuration model, and integration approach with the existing XD YARN deployment support.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Ambari service scripts (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Implement Python-based Ambari service scripts for installing, starting, stopping, and checking status of Spring XD admin and container components deployed on YARN.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Ambari configuration templates (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Create Ambari-managed configuration templates and property mapping for yarn-site, servers.yml, and Hadoop client configuration used by the XD-on-YARN deployment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.4",
      "activity_name": "Test Ambari-provisioned XD cluster on YARN (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Perform manual/system testing of cluster provisioning, start/stop, and basic XD job execution on a multi-node YARN cluster installed via Ambari.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.1",
      "activity_name": "Design spring-cloud-config integration for spring-bus (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Design how spring-bus modules bootstrap against a spring-cloud-config server, including bootstrap contexts and property precedence rules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement config client bootstrap in spring-bus modules (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement Spring Cloud Config client bootstrap integration in the spring-bus modules so external properties are fetched centrally at startup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.3",
      "activity_name": "Externalize bus/module properties to config server (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Move existing spring-bus and module properties into the Git-backed configuration served by the config server and adapt defaults.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.4",
      "activity_name": "Integration-test config server with bus implementations (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Integration-test centralized property management with the supported bus implementations (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka, Redis).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.1",
      "activity_name": "Set up channel performance benchmark harness (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Build a JMH-based benchmark harness exercising Spring Integration 4.2 channel types and configurations used by XD.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.2",
      "activity_name": "Benchmark, profile, and identify channel bottlenecks (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Run benchmarks and profiling sessions, analyze results, and identify concrete channel performance bottlenecks in SI 4.2 usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement corrective actions for channel bottlenecks (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the corrective code/configuration actions identified by the investigation, assumed limited to XD-side fixes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.4",
      "activity_name": "Verify improvements and write performance report (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Re-run benchmarks to confirm improvements and document findings, bottlenecks, and corrective actions taken.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.1",
      "activity_name": "Design serialization benchmark scenarios (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Define benchmark scenarios covering supported codecs/serializers, payload sizes, and representative XD module types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement serialization benchmark harness (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a repeatable benchmark harness measuring throughput and size characteristics of XD serialization options.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.3",
      "activity_name": "Measure baseline and report improvement areas (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Execute the measurements, analyze results, and produce the baseline report identifying areas of performance improvement.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.1",
      "activity_name": "Review spring-bus architecture and design specs (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Review the current spring-bus architecture, codebase, and design specifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.2",
      "activity_name": "Produce spring-bus gap analysis (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Document foundation-level gaps found in the review along with recommended remediation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.3",
      "activity_name": "Implement foundation-level gap fixes in spring-bus (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the agreed foundation-level gap fixes and small refactorings in spring-bus.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.1",
      "activity_name": "Implement RC-to-GA upgrade in Ambari plugin (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Spring XD 1.2 RC to 1.2 GA upgrade path in the Ambari plugin, including package replacement and configuration schema migration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.2",
      "activity_name": "Test Ambari upgrade scenarios (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Test upgrade scenarios from a fresh 1.2 RC install to 1.2 GA, verifying configuration preservation and cluster operability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.3",
      "activity_name": "Write upgrade user documentation (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Write the user-facing documentation describing how to perform the Ambari-based upgrade from 1.2 RC to 1.2 GA.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze fsUri handling in HDFS modules/jobs (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Analyze how fsUri is processed in the HDFS-aware modules and the jdbchdfs job to determine required changes for file:// support.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement LocalFileSystem support for file:// URIs (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement support for fsUri=file:// by relaxing HDFS-specific validation so Hadoop LocalFileSystem is used for local CSV ingestion scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.3",
      "activity_name": "Test file:// behavior and document caveat (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Test single-node file:// behavior end to end and document the multi-container local-file splitting caveat.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.1",
      "activity_name": "Design system-properties option for Sqoop job (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Design the module option used to pass JVM system properties (memory settings, connector options) to the Sqoop job process.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement property passing to spawned Sqoop JVM (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Implement appending the configured system properties to the command line of the separately spawned Sqoop Java process.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.3",
      "activity_name": "Test Sqoop system property propagation (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Test that memory and connector-related properties are correctly propagated and effective in the Sqoop job JVM.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.1",
      "activity_name": "Cross-story integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Perform integration testing across all delivered stories of the increment (Ambari install/upgrade with config-managed bus, jobs, and modules).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.2",
      "activity_name": "Build and CI updates",
      "activity_description": "Update build scripts and CI configuration for new modules, dependencies, and test suites introduced by the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.3",
      "activity_name": "Code reviews and rework",
      "activity_description": "Self-review and peer-review all changes across the eight stories and perform the resulting rework.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.4",
      "activity_name": "Final verification and release packaging support",
      "activity_description": "Perform final verification of the complete increment and support release packaging of the updated Spring XD distribution and Ambari plugin.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 56
  }
}

